---
import Docs from '../../layouts/Docs.astro'
import RecipeCard from '../../components/RecipeCard.astro'
import CommandTabs from '../../components/CommandTabs.astro'

const install = [
  { label: 'npm', code: 'npm i -D shotlist playwright' },
  { label: 'pnpm', code: 'pnpm add -D shotlist playwright' },
  { label: 'yarn', code: 'yarn add -D shotlist playwright' },
]

const scaffold = `npx shotlist --init`

const first = `npx shotlist example`

const missing = `Playwright is not installed. shotlist does not install it, because its
postinstall downloads browsers. Install it with:
  npm i -D playwright`
---

<Docs
  title="Install"
  description="Installing shotlist, why Playwright is a peer dependency, and scaffolding a first recipe."
>
  <h1 class="text-4xl font-extrabold">Install</h1>

  <p class="mt-6 leading-relaxed text-(--muted)">
    This is a <a
      href="https://nodejs.org/en/"
      title="Node.js website"
      target="_blank"
      rel="noopener noreferrer">Node.js</a
    > module available through the <a
      href="https://www.npmjs.com/"
      title="npm registry"
      target="_blank"
      rel="noopener noreferrer">npm</a
    >, <a
      href="https://yarnpkg.com/"
      title="yarn registry"
      target="_blank"
      rel="noopener noreferrer">yarn</a
    >, and <a
      href="https://pnpm.io/"
      title="pnpm registry"
      target="_blank"
      rel="noopener noreferrer">pnpm</a
    > registries. Before installing, <a
      href="https://nodejs.org/en/download/"
      title="Download Node.js"
      target="_blank"
      rel="noopener noreferrer">download and install Node.js</a
    >. Node.js 20 or higher is required. If this is a brand new project, make sure to create a <code
      >package.json</code
    > first with the <a
      href="https://docs.npmjs.com/cli/v8/commands/npm-init"
      title="npm init command"
      target="_blank"
      rel="noopener noreferrer"><code>npm init</code></a
    > command. Installation is done using the <a
      href="https://docs.npmjs.com/cli/v8/commands/npm-install"
      title="npm install command"
      target="_blank"
      rel="noopener noreferrer"><code>npm install</code></a
    > command:
  </p>

  <div class="mt-6">
    <CommandTabs commands={install} />
  </div>

  <h2 class="mt-14 text-2xl font-bold">When you need Playwright</h2>
  <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-(--muted)">
    <span class="font-medium text-ink">Whenever shotlist writes an image.</span>
    <code>npx shotlist &lt;name&gt;</code>,
    <code>--all</code> and
    <code>--check</code> all open a browser — including a
    <code>source: file</code> recipe, which drives no site but still draws its callouts in a page. In
    practice: install it alongside shotlist and stop thinking about it.
  </p>
  <p class="mt-5 leading-relaxed text-(--muted)">
    What runs without it is everything that only reads or writes files:
    <code>--init</code>,
    <code>--help</code>,
    <code>--version</code>, and
    <code>npx shotlist</code> with no arguments, which lists the recipes it found. A CI job that only
    checks a config parses needs no browser, and no browser is launched for it.
  </p>
  <p class="mt-5 leading-relaxed text-(--muted)">
    It is an optional peer dependency because its postinstall downloads browsers, and a project that
    depends on shotlist should not pay for that on every install — a CI cache, or a machine that
    only ever reads the recipes, gets nothing for it.
  </p>
  <p class="mt-5 leading-relaxed text-(--muted)">
    A run that needs a browser looks for
    <code>playwright</code>, then
    <code>playwright-core</code>, then the
    <code>npx</code> cache — which is what lets
    <code>npx shotlist</code> work in a project that has installed neither. Finding none of them it stops,
    before opening anything, with the command that fixes it:
  </p>
  <div class="mt-6">
    <RecipeCard code={missing} lang="bash" />
  </div>
  <p class="mt-6 leading-relaxed text-(--muted)">
    The browser is the first thing a run reaches for, so this arrives before any of the work rather
    than part-way through it. Nothing is written, and nothing is left half-done.
  </p>

  <h2 class="mt-14 text-2xl font-bold">A first recipe</h2>
  <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-(--muted)">
    <code>--init</code> writes a commented
    <code>shotlist.config.yaml</code> and a first recipe to edit. Neither is overwritten, so it is safe
    to run in a project that already has some.
  </p>
  <div class="mt-6">
    <RecipeCard code={scaffold} lang="bash" />
  </div>

  <p class="mt-6 leading-relaxed text-(--muted)">
    Start the site the config points at, then shoot it:
  </p>
  <div class="mt-6">
    <RecipeCard code={first} lang="bash" />
  </div>

  <p class="mt-6 leading-relaxed text-(--muted)">
    The image lands in <code>screenshots/out/</code>, and
    <code>--install</code> copies it to the destination the recipe names.
  </p>

  <p class="mt-10 leading-relaxed text-(--muted)">
    The recipe file carries a
    <code>yaml-language-server</code> line, so an editor completes and validates the keys from the JSON
    Schemas the package ships.
  </p>
</Docs>
